    fix(MCSP): compose the unary bound certificates explicitly
    
    After #671 made `fun_prop` infer composition encodings inner-first, the single
    `fun_prop` over the unfolded `s_bound` and `g` nests in
    `NEXP_subset_EXP_of_MCSP_npHard_of_EXP_subset_PPoly` hit the `whnf` heartbeat
    limit. Build `m_bound`, `s_bound` and `g` from the plain unary rules
    (`unary_add`, `unary_mul`, `unary_pow`, `id'`, `const`) through `comp` and
    `prod` instead, as LiuPass does for its threshold certificate. Proof-only: no
    statement changes.
    
    Coordinator fix-up for the PR authored by worker-jetski-9fbb7ac4.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Dvi6MU29zU9t8zYfeU51sB

